In Brazil, Germanic Studies lives above all in the Letras Alemão degrees and in graduate programs in Letras.

## What is studied

In practice, Germanists study everything from Goethe to Thomas Mann, analyze how German is spoken in Brazilian communities, translate works into Portuguese and train teachers. Many work between Brazil and German-speaking countries, in research partnerships and exchanges.

The main lines of the field are:

- **Literature** in German, from the Middle Ages to contemporary authors;
- **Linguistics** of German, including the varieties spoken in Brazil;
- **Translation** between German and Portuguese;
- **Teaching** German as a foreign language;
- **Cultural studies** and the relations between Brazil and German-speaking countries.

## Where to study Letras Alemão

The map of Letras Alemão programs in Brazil, with filters by state, is being prepared. Each program will link to the university's official page.

## What a Germanist does

Graduates of the field teach in schools and universities, translate, do research and work in culture, publishing and exchange. Explore the paths on the [Teaching](../ensino/) page.

## Join the community

Do you do research in Germanic Studies and are not yet an IVG member? See [how to join](../filiacao/).
